WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
What to carry forward.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:04.419
When you see a capability number, ask four questions.

3
00:00:04.699 --> 00:00:08.197
What does it measure, in what domain, at what reliability level?

4
00:00:08.477 --> 00:00:12.616
Is the benchmark saturated or contaminated, and has it been audited?

5
00:00:12.896 --> 00:00:16.373
Who ran it, with what scaffold and effort, and is there an interval?

6
00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:18.360
And what does it miss about your work?

7
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:29.413
METR’s horizon is the best single trend line available and it is running out of ruler; SWE-bench Verified’s retirement shows how quickly a trusted number goes stale.

8
00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:34.067
The next lesson uses these questions to choose models for real work.
